  "_meta": {
    "description": "Regional cultivation prior: which of the 22 modelled crops are actually cultivated in each state/UT, and at what scale. Compiled from Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare 'Agricultural Statistics at a Glance', APEDA/NHB horticulture area statistics, and state agriculture department cropping-pattern reports.",
    "why_this_exists": "The Kaggle crop-recommendation dataset is synthetic. Its feature envelopes are internally consistent but carry no geography, so a purely model-driven score will happily suggest mango for Ladakh or watermelon over coconut for Kerala. This layer supplies the geography the dataset lacks: the model scores agro-climatic fitness, this prior constrains the candidate set to crops the region demonstrably supports.",
    "tiers": {
      "major": "Significant cultivated area; established supply chain, mandi presence and extension support. Prior weight 1.0.",
      "minor": "Grown but on limited area, or confined to specific districts/agro-pockets. Prior weight 0.6.",
      "absent": "Not listed = not commercially cultivated in this state. Excluded from recommendation."
    },
    "limitation": "State-level granularity. A district-level prior (e.g. Nashik vs Vidarbha within Maharashtra) is the natural next iteration and is on the roadmap."
  },
